      <p><strong>Compact living</strong> is the choice to live in a smaller home, typically a tiny house of 100&ndash;400 sq ft or a small cottage, cabin or ADU under about 800 sq ft, and to design it so every square foot earns its place. The main advantages of tiny homes are lower costs (purchase, utilities, repairs and taxes), far less maintenance, a smaller environmental footprint and more freedom over where and how you live. The trade-offs are real too: less storage, less privacy, and zoning and financing hurdles. Below, we put numbers on each one so you can judge for yourself.</p>

